# Recorded packet results and limits

The client delivers one CSV-based packet workflow, using the joint pretrained model for prediction. These are retained experiments; copying the package or passing CPU CI is not a new GPU training run.

## Inputs and completed work

CICIDS2017 contains **1,410,255 rows**; UNSW contains **79,881**. Each row has 1,500 payload bytes, four metadata fields and a label. Every payload cell was validated. The neural model consumes bytes only: metadata/source identity are excluded from forward, and labels supply supervised targets only.

The adaptation uses the native four-block encoder, 378 tokens and a two-class head, with no observed size/interval sequences. Global payload hashes keep identical inputs in one partition across both sources. Contradictory labels remain as proportions. Training uses capped group subsets and replacement sampling.

All six native comparisons completed 1,000 updates with one model seed; all nine simple controls completed, including six converged logistic fits. Use the validation-selected joint pretrained model as the delivered classifier.

## Complete comparison table

Both columns below are **group-weighted balanced accuracy**: each distinct payload contributes total weight one, and benign/attack recall receive equal weight.

| Training source / initialization | CIC held-out test | UNSW held-out test |
|---|---:|---:|
| CIC / pretrained | 98.67% | 53.73% |
| CIC / scratch | 50.00% | 50.00% |
| UNSW / pretrained | 71.52% | 93.22% |
| UNSW / scratch | 50.00% | 50.00% |
| **Joint / pretrained** | **97.56%** | **94.29%** |
| Joint / scratch | 55.57% | 50.00% |

An UNSW-only metadata control reached **99.34%**, above every neural model on that test. The joint model's row-weighted balanced accuracy was 96.31% / 89.24%; counting repeated original rows changes the measure. Weak cross-source transfer and constant-class scratch results remain visible.

The two test sets contain 20,000 CIC and 5,930 UNSW groups. All 25,930 saved-model unlabeled classes matched primary evaluation; two strict raw-score comparisons failed. A later client-checkout check validated a 20,000-row CIC input and predicted its first 128 rows: all classes matched, but 76 strict score comparisons failed, with maximum absolute difference 0.006159305572509766. These are separate checks. [Later delivery receipt](https://github.com/buffbeefalo/netmambaplus-reproduction/blob/main/docs/research/client-edition-validation.json).

