## Relation to the paper and remaining work

The original paper consumes flows with bytes, sizes and time sequences. These CSV exports lack verified connection identity/order, so this project explicitly adapts its encoder to packets. The paper's 97.50% flow accuracy is not reproduced by these packet scores. Earlier separate flow experiments remain historical research in the full reproduction repo, not another client workflow.

One model seed, capped subsets, unknown pretrained exposure and unverified capture independence constrain the results. Selected CIC test support includes no PortScan and four DDoS rows. Packet scores are uncalibrated; customer-network performance, unknown-attack detection and operational alert thresholds are unestablished.

Native execution is measured on GB10. Live capture, a verified byte extractor, streaming/alert integration, complete-system throughput and NPU/SmartNIC execution remain future work. The earlier flow model's strict graph-export probe failed in a custom CUDA convolution; the packet adaptation retains custom kernels, and no successful packet export or accelerator port is claimed.
